## Context

Found by the roar sweep after PR #519 (ticket 0754's parity work). 0754
established, against zotero/zotero#6012's own `sdtTest.js`, that
`Zotero.SDT.ensure()` blocks and regenerates on a stale-processor pack rather
than backgrounding the work the way `getPack()` does. SYNC.md's "Zotero
extraction" drift-signal row said "a bump in the third silently re-extracts
existing packs in the background" — true of `getPack()`, not of `ensure()` —
and #519 corrected that row (`SYNC.md:516`) to name the distinction and cite
the pinned test.

`DECISIONS.md`'s 2026-09-03 entry ("The extraction-contract bound is
withdrawn: R1 does imply the treadmill") quotes the pre-correction wording
almost verbatim as its load-bearing premise: "`SYNC.md`'s Zotero extraction
row records that a `SDT_PROCESSOR_VERSIONS` bump silently re-extracts existing
packs, so under total supersession an unannounced upstream bump drains
extraction, chunking and embedding across the library on the user's machine,
unasked." That entry's actual conclusion — an unannounced upstream bump
drains the library unasked, so the drift watch is load-bearing — does not
depend on whether the drain is backgrounded or blocking, and this ticket is
not asking to reopen it. What needs the author's eye is narrower: the entry's
own wording now diverges from the source row it cites, and `DECISIONS.md` is
an append-only ledger (its own text, a few entries later: "this ledger is
append-only, so making 0590 the census would have falsified a ratified
sentence with no way to correct it") — a correction there needs a new entry,
not an edit in place, and a new entry needs the author's ratification the way
every other entry in that file does.

## Relevant files

- `DECISIONS.md` around the "2026-09-03 — The extraction-contract bound is
  withdrawn" entry — the citation to correct or annotate.
- `SYNC.md:516` — the corrected source row (ticket 0754, PR #519, merged
  2026-09-11), now distinguishing `getPack()`'s background regen from
  `ensure()`'s blocking one.
- `tickets/0754-audit-guarantee-parity-with-zotero-6012.erg` — the finding's
  origin (log entry, 2026-09-11).

## Actions

1. Author reads the 2026-09-03 DECISIONS.md entry against the corrected
   SYNC.md row and decides whether the citation needs a superseding note
   appended (ledger stays append-only — no in-place edit), and if so what it
   should say.
2. If a correction is warranted, append it in the same style as the file's
   existing supersession entries (e.g. the "extraction-contract bound is
   withdrawn" entry itself, which states what is withdrawn and what survives).

## Verification

- [ ] The appended entry (if any) is reviewed by the author before commit,
      consistent with every other entry in this ledger.

## Invariants

- `DECISIONS.md` stays append-only: no existing entry is edited or deleted.
- The entry's actual ratified conclusion (drift watch is load-bearing) is not
  disturbed by this ticket; only the citation's wording is in question.

## Exit criteria

Author has read the discrepancy and either appended a correction entry or
explicitly decided none is needed.
